{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you are commanded.</b> And tell them also that you have given them an order." "<b>Do this.</b> And to achieve this intended purpose — so that your father will not refuse to come (Genesis 45:27–28)." "<b>Take for yourselves from the land of Egypt wagons.</b> For when he sees the wagons ready, sent from us, he will find no grounds at all to refuse and decline. And so it was afterward, as he said: <b>And he saw the wagons which Joseph had sent to carry him, and Israel said: I will go and see him</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:47.065862887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}